================================================================================
  CONF.YAML CHANGES IN DELL EMC ISILON CUSTOM BUILD (v3.6.0)
  Crest Data Systems -- Dell EMC Isilon Custom Build
================================================================================

WHAT CHANGED
------------
  One new option, zone_export_ids, collects NFS export statistics from the
  access zones you list. All other options are unchanged. The installation
  does not change your existing conf.yaml, so add the option yourself.

HOW TO USE
----------
  1. Add zone_export_ids to the instance of each cluster in conf.yaml:

       instances:
         - ip_address: <CLUSTER_IP_ADDRESS>
           username: <USERNAME>
           password: <PASSWORD>
           port: '8080'
           min_collection_interval: 120
           zone_export_ids:
             NGIC-NFS: ""
             NGLS-NFS: ""

  2. Restart the Datadog Agent.

VALUE OF EACH ACCESS ZONE
-------------------------
  ""        Collect all exports of the zone.
  "1,3"     Collect only export IDs 1 and 3 of the zone.
  "-2,-4"   Collect all exports of the zone except export IDs 2 and 4.

  Export IDs are unique only within an access zone, so they are set per zone.

RULES
-----
  - Only the listed zones are collected. Add  System: ""  to also collect the
    System zone.
  - A zone cannot have both export IDs to collect and export IDs to exclude.
  - zone_export_ids cannot be used together with export_ids. If export_ids is
    set, remove it and set the export IDs per zone instead.

IN DATADOG
----------
  NFS metrics have a new tag, cds.emc.isilon.zone (shown in lowercase), and
  the NFS Export Stats dashboard has a new Zone filter.

